{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["<b>Every one that opens the womb is Mine.</b> In man." "<b>And all your cattle, etc.</b> וְכָל מִקְנְךָ אֲשֶׁר תִּזָּכָר בְּפֶטֶר שׁוֹר וָשֶׂה — that a male opens its womb." "<b>Opens.</b> A term of opening, as in ״פּוֹטֵר מַיִם רֵאשִׁית מָדוֹן״ (Proverbs 17). The tav of תִּזָּכָר is feminine, referring back to the one giving birth."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 34, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:32.750804250Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}